Inscription:
Inscription type: inscription Inscription position: exterior Inscription script: hieroglyphic Inscription transliteration: pr-nsw 
ḥwt Ḥr p w‘ỉ 
ḥwt zʒ ḥʒ nb Inscription note: Incised. For bibliography on ḥwt Ḥr p w‘ỉ , see P. Kaplony, 'Die Inschriften der Ägyptischen Frühzeit I (Wiesbaden, 1963) 816-817, 858-861, 1126. The building ḥwt zʒ ḥʒ nb occurs on numerous inscriptions, and has been interpreted by Kaplony as a royal palace at Memphis (P. Kaplony, 'Die Inschriften der Ägyptischen Frühzeit II (Wiesbaden, 1964), anm. 809-10, 813, 992, 1405, 1781. Kaplony reads the name simply as ḥwt zʒ ḥʒ). See also P. Lacau & J. P . Lauer, 'Pyramide à degrees IV, fasc. 2, 26, no. 46; 31-2, no. 58; 54, no. 108; R. Weill, ‘Recherches sur la première dynastie et les temps prépharaoniques (Cairo, 1961),  136-41; F. LI. Griffith, in W. M. F. Petrie, 'Royal Tombs of the Earliest Dynasties' I, 40.; Inscription type: inscription Inscription position: exterior Inscription script: hieroglyphic Inscription transliteration: bỉtỉ Inscription note: At the extreme right-hand edge of the fragment, is part of the bỉtỉ sign, where the group nsw bỉtỉ nbty ḳ(ʒ)‘ would have stood. For similar inscriptions, see W. M. F. Petrie, 'Royal Tombs of the Earliest Dynasties' I, pl.IX, 2, 4, 5; P. Lacau & J. P . Lauer, 'Pyramide à degrees IV, fasc. 1, pl.IV, 8-11 (cf. , pl.IV, 7).; Inscription type: inscription Inscription position: exterior Inscription script: hieroglyphic Inscription translation: Signs of an uncertain meaning. Inscription note: Incised. Taken to be a name, Hetep-renpet, in P. Kaplony, 'Die Inschriften der Ägyptischen Frühzeit I (Wiesbaden, 1963), 593-4.;

