Inscription type: inscription Inscription position: right edge Inscription script: hieroglyphic Inscription transliteration: rnpt 
šmsw- Ḥr 
Ḥḏ-wrw Inscription translation: Reference to the festivals of Shemsu-Hor and Hedj-wer Inscription note: Incised. For Ḥḏ-wrw, see H. W. Fairman, 'Annales du Service des Antiquitiés de l'Égypte' 43 (1943), 260-3; R. Weill, ‘Recherches sur la première dynastie et les temps prépharaoniques’ II, 96-9; P. Kaplony, ‘Kleine Beiträge zu den Inschriften der Ägyptischen Frühzeit’ (Wiesbaden, 1966), 92-6.; Inscription type: inscription Inscription position: left side Inscription script: hieroglyphic Inscription translation: The royal name Irynetjer (nsw-bỉtỉ nbty ‘Iry-nṯr) and the name of the official, Henuka, who has the title mḏḥty-nsw. Inscription note: Incised. Separated from right-hand inscription by a vertical red dividing line. Kapolny reads Henuka's title as mḏḥ-mḏḥ(w) nsw, see P. Kaplony, 'Die Inschriften der Ägyptischen Frühzeit I (Wiesbaden, 1963), 300.; Inscription type: inscription Inscription position: bottom Inscription script: hieroglyphic Inscription translation: The name to the type of oil contained within the jar. Inscription note: Incised. See P. Kaplony, 'Die Inschriften der Ägyptischen Frühzeit I (Wiesbaden, 1963), 305.; Inscription type: inscription Inscription position: top left-hand corner Inscription script: hieroglyphic Inscription note: Incised. The signs have been variously interpreted, but may denote an administrative building. See P. Kaplony, 'Die Inschriften der Ägyptischen Frühzeit II (Wiesbaden, 1964), 1008-9, n. 1616. Kaplony reads these signs as 'ḫtỉw', see P. Kaplony, 'Die Inschriften der Ägyptischen Frühzeit I (Wiesbaden, 1963), 299.;

