A similar label, also from Abydos, completes the missing portions of this example, see Petrie, 'Royal Tombs of the Earliest Dynasties' II, pls. IIIA, 5; X, 2; H. Ranke, 'The Egyptian Collections of the University Museum Philadelphia' (1950), fig. 11; F. Legge, ‘Proceedings of the Society of Biblical Archaeology’ 29 (London,1907), pl. opp. p.24, no. 2; J. Vandier, 'Manuel d'Archeologie egyptienne', I, (2), 836-40 and fig. 560. The scenes on these two labels have been considered to refer to the visit of Aḥa to the temple of Neith at Sais. and to the creation of the ỉmy-wt symbol; see the discussions in the above references and also R. Weill, ‘Recherches sur la première dynastie et les temps prépharaoniques I (Cairo, 1961) , 157; R. Weill, ‘Recherches sur la première dynastie et les temps prépharaoniques II (Cairo, 1961), 1-5, 48-9: V. Vikentiev,  'Annales du Service des Antiquitiés de l'Égypte' 41 (1942), 285-7; P. Kaplony, 'Die Inschriften der Ägyptischen Frühzeit' II (Wiesbaden, 1964), 989, n. 1565; Sethe, 'Untersuchungen' III, 62; G. Jequier, ‘Bulletin de l’Institut Français d’Archéologie Orientale’ 6(Cairo, 1908), 27-31; W. S. Smith, 'History of Egyptian Sculpture and Painting in the Old Kingdom' (London, 1946), 120, no. 4.
